Homelab Proxmox network reference

Host: {{ inventory_hostname }}
LAN physical NIC: {{ proxmox_lan_physical_nic }}
LAN bridge: {{ proxmox_lan_bridge_name }}
WAN physical NIC: {{ proxmox_wan_physical_nic }}
WAN bridge: {{ proxmox_wan_bridge_name }}
Bootstrap management IP: {{ ansible_host }}
Bootstrap gateway: {{ legacy_flat_lan_gateway }}
Management VLAN: {{ proxmox_management_vlan_id }}
Cutover management IP: {{ pve_management_ip | default('REPLACE_WITH_PVE_MANAGEMENT_IP') }}
Management subnet: {{ proxmox_management_subnet }}
Management gateway: {{ proxmox_management_gateway }}
Trunk VLANs: {{ proxmox_trunk_vlans | join(', ') }}
Flat Wi-Fi VLAN: {{ proxmox_flat_wifi_vlan_id }}
Netgear AP switch mode: {{ proxmox_flat_wifi_ap_mode }}

Stage 1 bootstrap:
- Keep Proxmox management on the current flat LAN.
- Make {{ proxmox_lan_bridge_name }} VLAN-aware without changing the management subnet.
- Create {{ proxmox_wan_bridge_name }} for the dedicated WAN NIC without assigning an IP.

Stage 2 cutover:
- Move Proxmox management to VLAN {{ proxmox_management_vlan_id }}.
- Use gateway {{ proxmox_management_gateway }} after OPNsense is live.
- OPNsense receives a LAN trunk from {{ proxmox_lan_bridge_name }}.
- OPNsense receives direct WAN handoff from {{ proxmox_wan_bridge_name }}.
- Netgear LAX20 stays on flat client LAN access mode only.

Reference only. Apply network changes deliberately from console access.
